// `++=` appends to the list in `values[0]` in place, yet its result is still
// stored back: `ListIndex` reads the element into r4, `CallNative` of `++=`
// puts the result in r3, and `ListSet` stores r3 at `values[0]`. The container
// and index are read once, into r1 and r2, where both instructions read them.
// compile: stdlib
let value = [1]; let values = [value]; values[0] ++= [2];
